#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""mesh-novelty — a Shannon-surprise signal over the mesh's own event stream.

Well-studied field: information theory. The self-information of an event is
I(x) = -log2 P(x): rare/new events carry many bits, routine events carry few.
The mesh emits hundreds of routine lines ([done], [taking], [git-lock]) and a
handful of rare ones ([gap], [incident], [health-fail], a never-seen tag, a
first-seen device). Without a measure, the operator drowns in noise and the
mesh wakes expensive minds for nothing.

mesh-novelty reads the board (and presence), learns the BASELINE distribution
of event types, and scores a RECENT window:
  - per-event surprisal under the baseline (add-1 smoothed; a NEW type = max bits)
  - an aggregate novelty score (mean bits of the window)
  - the specific high-surprise events + first-seen entities (devices/tools/errors)

Why it matters (two payoffs, both real):
  1. LEGIBILITY — after an absence, "what was genuinely NEW vs routine" in one
     line, so the digest surfaces signal not 200 lines of noise.
  2. SPEND — a cheap reflex can gate expensive minds: wake on HIGH novelty,
     stay silent on routine. (Attention follows information, not volume.)

  mesh-novelty                 report novelty of the recent window vs baseline
  mesh-novelty --window N      recent window = N board lines (default 40)
  mesh-novelty --threshold B   stream mode: print a feed line only if score >= B bits
  mesh-novelty --edge          edge-triggered: emit only on mean shift >±0.5b or new top-5
  mesh-novelty --edge --min-gap S  + a min-interval floor: hold a real edge if the last
                               emit was < S sec ago (the change still fires once S elapses)
  mesh-novelty --conditional   (alias --ctx) score CONTEXTUAL prediction error, not marginal
                               rarity — combines with the report / --threshold / --edge
  mesh-novelty --diversity     Shannon-evenness of the BASELINE type distribution's SHAPE
                               (not per-event surprisal — see DIVERSITY section below)
  mesh-novelty --levels        LOCAL-GLOBAL two-timescale deviance (report-only; --json for the
                               dict) — classify each recent event as REGIME-ONSET/LOCAL-BLIP/etc
  mesh-novelty --territory     DETERRITORIALIZATION COEFFICIENT (report-only; --json) — split the
                               window early/late and classify each surprising surge as RELATIVE
                               (recaptured — snaps back) vs ABSOLUTE (a line of flight — not recaptured)
  mesh-novelty --bayesian      BAYESIAN SURPRISE (Itti & Baldi; report-only; --json; alias --wow) — score
                               each recent type by how much it MOVES the belief (KL of the Dirichlet
                               update), not how improbable it is; flags HABITUATED types (high Shannon,
                               ~zero belief-move — a wake raw surprisal over-pays every recurrence) vs
                               genuinely MODEL-MOVING ones. Attention follows belief-update, not rarity.
  mesh-novelty --test          smoke test

DIVERSITY (LITERATURE, live review 2026-07-02: biosemiotics — sign and meaning in living
systems, angle=a concrete METRIC this area uses to measure itself). Everything above scores
an INDIVIDUAL event against the baseline. It never asks a different, biosemiotically-real
question: does the baseline's own type-frequency distribution have the SHAPE of a working
sign repertoire at all? Zoosemiotic/bioacoustic work quantifies this: real communication
repertoires (animal call types, word frequencies) follow a Zipfian rank-frequency skew — a
few common signs, many rare ones — and Shannon entropy of the repertoire is used as a
ROBUST estimator of that skew because direct log-log slope-fitting is unreliable on the
small sample sizes typical of both animal-call corpora and (here) a ~40-line window
(Kershenbaum et al., "Shannon entropy as a robust estimator of Zipf's Law in animal vocal
communication repertoires", Methods in Ecology and Evolution 2021, 10.1111/2041-210X.13536;
recent grounding: "Linguistic laws in biology", arXiv:2310.07387; "For a semiotic of opacity:
the role of biosemiotics between AI and animal communication", 2025, applying this exact
skew-vs-uniform lens to critique AI animal-communication decoders). The counterintuitive
operational reading: a Zipfian code is markedly UNEVEN by construction (dominant + long
tail), so an event-type distribution trending toward UNIFORM (every marker equally likely)
is the anomaly, not the healthy state — the mesh's board vocabulary ([done]/[idle] common,
[incident]/[gap] rare) is expected to sit LOW-TO-MID on the evenness scale; a spike toward
BOTH extremes is diagnostic: near-0 evenness (an existing memory: [[operator-msg-board-broadcast-floods-responders]],
verbose-idle/phantom-taking floods) means the marker vocabulary has collapsed to a
monoculture, and near-1 evenness means posts are firing with no differentiated code at all
(pure noise, not a working repertoire). `diversity()` below reuses the SAME `base` Counter
`analyse()` already builds (no new data collection) — distinct from mean_bits (an event's
individual surprise) and from the eigenform/volatility/noisy-TV HELD blocks in analyse()
(those score dynamics of INDIVIDUAL scores over time; this scores the STATIC shape of the
distribution those scores are drawn from). Shipped as an opt-in `--diversity` flag, NOT
folded into the default `fmt()` text several tools already grep
([[cross-sense-vocab-contract]]: changing default sense output silently breaks consumers).

PREDICTIVE-CODING UPGRADE (live review 2026-06-20: predictive processing & the Bayesian brain
— a foundational idea we applied TOO LOOSELY). Predictive coding does NOT measure surprise as a
signal's marginal rarity; it transmits only the RESIDUAL against a CONTEXTUAL forward prediction
("explaining away" / repetition suppression — Millidge et al., "Predictive Coding: A Theoretical
and Experimental Review", arXiv:2107.12979; "Repetition suppression and its contextual determinants
in predictive coding", Cortex 2016; current framing: "The Information-Theoretic Imperative",
arXiv:2510.25883, 2025 — "transmit what is surprising rather than what is predicted"). The DEFAULT
score above is MARGINAL surprisal -log P(eᵢ): a [done] that ALWAYS follows [taking] (perfectly
predictable, ~0 true prediction error) scores identically to a [done] arriving with NO preceding
[taking] (genuinely unpredicted). That conflates rarity with surprise. --conditional scores the
predictive-coding quantity -log P(eᵢ | eᵢ₋₁) via a first-order Markov forward model over the
baseline: a predictable sequence is "explained away" (low bits → don't wake minds), a contextually
UNexpected transition scores high (wake). Default stays marginal (back-compat); consumers opt in.
This is distinct from PRECISION-weighting (scripts/mesh-precision, landed 2026-06-20) — that
weights HOW reliable a signal is; this measures WHETHER a signal was predicted from context.
"""
# ── review-fep-dark-room-prior-preference-2026-07-27 (LIVE literature — a CRITIQUE / failure mode) ──
# TASK: FEP / Active Inference (Friston) from the angle of a known CRITIQUE. The mesh has already landed
# the major critiques — the Emperor's-New-Markov-Blankets / Pearl-vs-Friston reification (mesh-perimeter),
# the small-world / frame-problem limit of relevance-realization (mesh-precision: Jaeger 2024,
# Parvizi-Wayne 2025), and the NOISY-TV / curiosity-trap (this file, 2026-06-21). The one canonical FEP
# failure mode NOT yet embodied is its most-cited: the DARK-ROOM PROBLEM.
#
# THE FAILURE MODE — the DARK ROOM. If a system minimises SURPRISE, why not seek the most predictable
# environment possible — a dark, silent, unchanging room — and stay there? A pure surprise-minimiser
# prefers predictable input, so it goes BLIND to a condition once that condition becomes predictable.
# This file IS a surprise-minimiser used as a SPEND gate ("wake on HIGH novelty, stay silent on
# routine"), and its own analyse() header already documents the dark-room in local form — the
# boiling-frog / eigenform ABSORPTION note: a persistent [health-fail]/[incident] recurs, accretes into
# `base`, its p(t) rises, its surprisal -log P FALLS, and it STOPS waking minds exactly because it is now
# chronic. That HELD fix was blocked because "a real regime change looks identical to a pathological
# accretion — separating them needs a reference the loop does NOT author."
#
# THE MECHANISM (the FEP's OWN resolution to the dark room) — PRIOR PREFERENCES. The FEP answer is that
# agents do not minimise raw surprise; they minimise surprise relative to PREFERRED observations (goal
# priors / the "C" vector) — outcomes they act to obtain (and to keep observing) even when unsurprising.
# Those preferences are DESIGN-SPECIFIED, not learned from the agent's own sensory history — which is
# precisely the "reference the loop does not author" the HELD note needed. So prior preferences unblock
# the absorption failure for the critical SUBSET (a curated must-attend tag set), while the GENERAL
# regime-change-vs-accretion problem stays correctly HELD (this does not touch it).
#   LIVE SOURCES (read 2026-07-27, current lit — not a fixed list):
#     • Karl Friston, Christopher Thornton, Andy Clark, "Free-energy minimization and the dark-room
#       problem", Frontiers in Psychology 3:130 (2012) — the canonical statement + the prior-preference
#       resolution. https://www.frontiersin.org/articles/10.3389/fpsyg.2012.00130
#     • Filippo Torresan, Ryota Kanai, Manuel Baltieri, "Prior preferences in active inference agents:
#       soft, hard, and goal shaping", arXiv:2512.03293 (Dec 2025) — the CURRENT treatment of HOW to
#       specify these preferences: hard (sharp) priors are brittle, soft/shaped priors are robust.
#       (The mesh already has the "by-name poke must-answer" floor on the room organ — same principle,
#       different organ; this extends the must-attend floor to the novelty spend-gate.)
#
# THE ONE CONCRETE APPLICATION (this edit): a PRIOR-PREFERENCE FLOOR. A design-specified must-attend tag
# set (MESH_NOVELTY_PREF_TAGS, default `incident health-fail gap`) is surfaced by analyse() as `pref_hits`
# WHATEVER its surprisal, shown by fmt() even on a "routine" window, and fires the --threshold wake gate
# regardless of mean_bits — deduped by TIME (re-assert every MESH_NOVELTY_PREF_REFRESH, default 1h) so a
# chronic critical condition is never permanently absorbed nor spammed each cron. The surprise MEASUREMENT
# is left PURE (mean_bits/scored untouched — no silent inflation); the floor is a parallel, labelled
# attend-regardless channel. RED-first test: a chronic [health-fail] absorbed to <4b still lands in
# pref_hits; MESH_NOVELTY_PREF_TAGS="" empties the set and the assertion goes red.
import sys, os, re, math, time
from collections import Counter

MESH = os.path.expanduser("~/.mesh")
CHAT = os.path.join(MESH, "chat.log")
PRESENCE = os.path.join(MESH, "presence.log")

TAG = re.compile(r'\[([a-z][a-z-]*)\]')
MAC = re.compile(r'\b([0-9A-Fa-f]{2}(?::[0-9A-Fa-f]{2}){5})\b')

BOARD = re.compile(r'^\d{2,4}[-:0-9T]*Z?\s+\S+\s+::')   # a real dated board line

# ── PRIOR-PREFERENCE FLOOR (active-inference dark-room fix) — see the header review block ──────────
# A DESIGN-SPECIFIED (not board-learned) set of must-attend tags: a preferred/critical observation the
# mind attends REGARDLESS of surprise. Because the set is not harvested from the board's own history, it
# CANNOT be absorbed into the baseline the way the boiling-frog / eigenform HELD note in analyse()
# describes — that is exactly why it unblocks the absorption failure for this critical subset.
PREF_TAGS = set(t for t in os.environ.get("MESH_NOVELTY_PREF_TAGS", "incident health-fail gap").split() if t)
PREF_REFRESH = int(os.environ.get("MESH_NOVELTY_PREF_REFRESH", "3600"))  # re-assert cadence (s): a chronic
                                                                         # must-attend re-fires every hour,
                                                                         # never once-then-silent, never spam

# ── LOCAL–GLOBAL TWO-TIMESCALE DEVIANCE (predictive-processing local-global paradigm) ──────────────
# LITERATURE (live review 2026-07-27, angle = a concrete EXPERIMENT this area measures itself with):
# the LOCAL-GLOBAL oddball paradigm (Bekinschtein, Dehaene, Rohaut, Tadel, Cohen, Naccache, "Neural
# signature of the conscious processing of auditory regularities", PNAS 106:1672, 2009) — still the
# 2024-2025 workhorse for dissociating hierarchical levels of prediction error: a stimulus can be a
# LOCAL deviant (violates the last few items, short timescale, ~150 ms, automatic/feedforward,
# attention-independent) while being a GLOBAL standard (conforms to the block's established long-range
# rule, ~seconds, attention-dependent, top-down) — and vice-versa. The two dissociate in cortical
# locus, latency and consciousness-sensitivity. CURRENT: Jamali et al., "Parallel mechanisms signal a
# hierarchy of sequence structure violations in the auditory cortex", eLife 2025 (10.7554/eLife.102702)
# — local & global violations are signalled by PARALLEL, separable mechanisms, not one cascade; and
# "Localizing hierarchical prediction errors and precisions during an oddball task with volatility",
# Imaging Neuroscience 2025 (10.1162/imag_a_00461). THE GAP: this reflex scores every recent event's
# surprisal against ONE baseline (the long history `base`). It cannot dissociate a LOCAL-deviant-but-
# GLOBAL-standard blip (a routine type merely absent from the immediate context, then reappearing —
# the automatic local oddball, low wake value) from a LOCAL-standard-but-GLOBAL-deviant REGIME ONSET
# (a type rare in long history yet ALREADY RECURRING in the immediate window — an anomaly forming). The
# regime-onset case is the eigenform-absorption HELD block's COMPLEMENT caught at ONSET: eigenform flags
# the accretion AFTER the baseline has absorbed it (frequency rising across baselines, marginal surprise
# fallen); this flags it WHILE still global-rare but already local-recurring — i.e. before absorption.
# Report-only (does NOT touch the wake gate — the SPEND wiring stays the steward's, like the sibling
# HELD fixes); distinct from HGF-volatility (scales the bar by change-RATE) and the prior-preference
# floor (a design-fixed must-attend tag set). Two nested baselines: GLOBAL = long history `base`;
# LOCAL = the recent window minus its tip (the immediate short-timescale context).
LEVELS_TIP = int(os.environ.get("MESH_NOVELTY_LEVELS_TIP", "5"))     # # of most-recent events classified
LEVELS_HI  = float(os.environ.get("MESH_NOVELTY_LEVELS_HI", "4.0"))  # deviance bar (bits) — reuses the surprise bar

# ── DETERRITORIALIZATION COEFFICIENT: RELATIVE (recaptured) vs ABSOLUTE (line of flight) ────────────
# LITERATURE (live review 2026-07-28 — Deleuze & Guattari, assemblage/rhizome/machinic, angle = a
# concrete MEASURE the field uses on itself; doc: docs/reviews/deleuze-deterritorialization-coefficient-
# relative-vs-absolute-recapture-2026-07-28.md). D&G is a well-worked mesh seam (rhizome→mesh-sensor-tape,
# territorialization/DeLanda→mesh-digest, refrain→mesh-reflex-health, order-word→board, smooth/striated
# →velocity+distance, disjunctive-synthesis→mesh-situation). The one axis NOT embodied is the field's own
# MEASURE of a movement: the COEFFICIENT of deterritorialization, and its RELATIVE-vs-ABSOLUTE cut.
#
# THE MEASURE — every deterritorialization (an element ESCAPING its coded territory) has a coupled
# RETERRITORIALIZING edge, and the two uses are distinguished by RECAPTURE (Thornton, "On Lines of Flight",
# RHUL PhD 2018, pp.196-197, reading ATP 359 & 62): a RELATIVE (negative) deterritorialization is one where
# the assemblage "only changes in relation to a given form of stability that it maintains over time" — the
# escape is RECAPTURED, it snaps back; an ABSOLUTE (positive) deterritorialization — a LINE OF FLIGHT — is
# one where "one leaves all assemblages behind... entering another plane", the prior organisation is
# destroyed and NOT recaptured (ATP: relative D. is "stratic or interstratic", absolute D. "concern[s] the
# plane of consistency and its destratification"). So a surge is a line of flight ONLY if it is not pulled
# back — magnitude alone (a big surprise) does not tell you which; PERSISTENCE-past-the-reterritorializing-
# edge does. Guattari names the measurable form directly — the "coefficient of transversality", a group's
# tunable degree of openness-to-escape (Guattari, "Transversality", 1964 / Psychoanalysis & Transversality).
#
# THE GAP THIS NAMES — every axis on this file scores a surge's MAGNITUDE or its timescale at ONE moment:
# marginal surprisal (rarity NOW), --conditional (contextual residual NOW), --levels (short-vs-long deviance
# NOW). NONE asks the D&G question: did the surge STAY, or did the board's distribution RETERRITORIALIZE back
# to its prior shape? A one-shot spike that snaps back (a flapping sense, a burst that self-resolves) is a
# RELATIVE deterritorialization — low wake value — yet it reads MAX bits and (use-case-2) can wake a mind.
# The recapture read distinguishes it from an ABSOLUTE line of flight (a genuine new regime the board did
# NOT return from). DISTINCT from the two HELD blocks in analyse(): eigenform-absorption is the SAME type's
# surprise FALLING as it accretes across baselines (a false negative, needs a reference the loop can't
# author); this is the COMPLEMENT that IS self-authored — the reference is simply TIME-FORWARD recapture,
# observable on the board with a lag, no oracle. It does not judge whether an absolute shift is GOOD (that
# stays the steward's, like the siblings); it only measures relative-vs-absolute. Report-only, opt-in
# --territory; does NOT touch the wake gate (instrument-first, same discipline as --levels/--diversity).
ESCAPE_MIN = float(os.environ.get("MESH_NOVELTY_ESCAPE_MIN", "0.1"))  # min early-half freq-gain over baseline
BAYES_FRAC = float(os.environ.get("MESH_NOVELTY_BAYES_FRAC", "0.5"))   # frac of a NEW type's belief-move to call MODEL-MOVING
                                                                     # to count as a deterritorializing surge

def read_lines(path):
    try:
        with open(path, encoding="utf-8", errors="replace") as f:
            raw = [l.rstrip("\n") for l in f if l.strip()]
    except FileNotFoundError:
        return []
    # keep only well-formed board lines (drops the undated legacy philosophy/task dump that
    # otherwise sits at the file's physical end and pollutes the 'recent' window)
    board = [l for l in raw if BOARD.match(l)]
    return board if path == CHAT else raw

def event_type(line):
    """Coarse event signature: the bracket tag, else a generic class."""
    m = TAG.search(line)
    if m:
        return m.group(1)
    if "::" in line and "@" in line.split("::")[0]:
        return "_chat"          # an un-tagged board utterance
    return "_other"

def surprisal(p):
    return -math.log2(p) if p > 0 else 0.0

def _digamma(x):
    """ψ(x) via recurrence up to x≥6 + Abramowitz-Stegun 6.3.18 asymptotic (~1e-6 for x≥1).
    numpy-free (this tool has no numpy dep and must keep it): scipy.special.digamma is the
    reference, reimplemented here in stdlib. Anchored in --test at ψ(1)=−γ and ψ(2)=1−γ."""
    r = 0.0
    while x < 6.0:
        r -= 1.0 / x
        x += 1.0
    f = 1.0 / (x * x)
    return r + math.log(x) - 0.5 / x - f * (1/12.0 - f * (1/120.0 - f * (1/252.0)))

def bayes_bits(alpha_t, A):
    """BAYESIAN SURPRISE (Itti & Baldi) in BITS of observing ONE more event of a type whose
    current Dirichlet pseudo-count is alpha_t, total concentration A: the KL between the
    posterior Dir(α+eₜ) and the prior Dir(α). Closed form for a unit categorical update:
        KL[posterior‖prior] = ln A − ln αₜ + ψ(αₜ+1) − ψ(A+1)      (nats)
    This is how much the BELIEF MOVES, NOT how improbable the datum was (that is Shannon
    surprise −log p). The two dissociate: a KNOWN-rare type under a mature baseline has HIGH
    Shannon surprise every recurrence yet ~0 belief-move (you already know rare things happen);
    a first-seen type moves the belief maximally. KL ≥ 0 always — clamp guards digamma slop."""
    nats = math.log(A) - math.log(alpha_t) + _digamma(alpha_t + 1.0) - _digamma(A + 1.0)
    return max(0.0, nats) / math.log(2.0)

def analyse(window=40, conditional=False):
    lines = read_lines(CHAT)
    if len(lines) < 10:
        return None
    recent = lines[-window:]
    # ── EIGENFORM / DEGENERATE-FIXED-POINT BLIND SPOT (von Foerster; Kauffman) ───────────────────
    # 2nd-order cybernetics cross-domain transfer (LITERATURE 2026-06-21): von Foerster — "objects
    # are tokens for EIGENBEHAVIORS"; an object/state is the stable FIXED POINT of the observer's own
    # recursive operation, T(Object)=Object (Kauffman, "Eigenforms — Objects as Tokens for
    # Eigenbehaviors", Cybernetics & Human Knowing, 2003-05; von Foerster, "Objects: Tokens for
    # (Eigen-)Behaviors", 1976). The deep point: the observer is PART of the observed, so a
    # self-referential signal can converge to a fixed point that has DECOUPLED from the world.
    #
    # THIS function is reflexive in exactly that sense: the baseline IS the system's OWN past output
    # (lines[:-window] of the same board mesh-novelty also writes to via --edge/--stream). That makes
    # the novelty score an eigenform of a self-observing loop — and it has the UNDER-COVERED failure
    # mode (the COUPLED-but-decoupling direction, sibling to the honest-fusion DECOUPLED guards):
    #   • A PERSISTENT anomaly is ABSORBED into "normal." Once a pathological event type recurs across
    #     enough lines it accretes into `base` (below) → its p(t) rises → its surprisal -log P FALLS →
    #     it stops being novel. The baseline becomes its own confirmation: a DEGENERATE fixed point
    #     (reproduces regardless of whether the thing is actually a problem). Boiling-frog / self-
    #     confirmation. Neither marginal surprisal NOR --edge catches it: a gradual accretion slips
    #     under the ±0.5b shift floor, and absorption LOWERS mean novelty (--edge watches for a rise).
    # VERIFIED THIS SESSION: the home_state↔desk re-flood — the SAME spurious CORRELATION/CONNECTION
    # dispatch + [done] hit the board 4× (10:12/10:15/10:29/11:02). After the first 1-2, those types
    # are in the baseline → the 3rd/4th score LOW novelty. A human caught the pathological RECURRENCE
    # by reasoning; this reflex structurally CANNOT — its baseline self-confirmed. (The seed-laundering
    # fix in mesh-correlate stopped the SOURCE; this names why the novelty SENSE was blind to it.)
    #
    # HELD FIX (instrument-first, steward/operator lands — behavioral): add a SECOND axis beside
    # surprisal-vs-baseline — a BASELINE-DRIFT / eigenform-stability check: flag an event type whose
    # frequency is RISING across successive baselines (an anomaly accreting into normal) even as its
    # marginal surprise falls. I.e. test whether the baseline is itself a STABLE fixed point or is
    # absorbing — a persistent-anomaly detector is the exact complement to a rare-event detector.
    # WHY HELD: a real regime change (the mesh genuinely growing a new normal) looks identical to a
    # pathological accretion at the signal level — separating them needs a reference the loop does NOT
    # author (a fixed long-baseline, or operator/queue-tend confirmation), else it just flags all
    # growth. Validate against the board history before gating a SPEND signal (this gates mind wake).
    # See [[fusion-tools-distinguish-empty-from-failed]] (DECOUPLED dir), [[delta-channels-need-gate]],
    # [[review-coupling-constitution-fallacy-mesh-card-2026-06-21]] (the membership-direction sibling).
    #
    # ── VOLATILITY-BLIND THRESHOLD: the wake bar is FIXED; it should track environmental change-rate ──
    # LITERATURE (live review, what's NEW in predictive processing 2023-2026): the Bayesian-brain
    # frontier most used right now is the HIERARCHICAL GAUSSIAN FILTER (Mathys et al., "A Bayesian
    # foundation for individual learning under uncertainty", Front. Hum. Neurosci. 2011; "Uncertainty in
    # perception and the HGF", 2014) — still the 2023-2026 workhorse of computational psychiatry, where
    # aberrant VOLATILITY estimation indexes psychosis/hallucination (precision-weighted prediction-error
    # studies, biorxiv 2025.07.07.662254; Frontiers Psychiatry 2025, fpsyt.2025.1713833). The HGF's key
    # move beyond flat precision-weighting: a HIGHER level that tracks how fast the hidden cause is
    # CHANGING (volatility), and the learning-rate / surprise-bar is scaled by it — in a VOLATILE regime a
    # big delta is EXPECTED (low surprise, learn slowly), in a STABLE regime the same delta is alarming
    # (high surprise, learn fast). Precision = inverse variance of the signal NOW; volatility = variance of
    # the GENERATIVE rate-of-change over time. Two different levels of the same hierarchy.
    #
    # THE GAP THIS NAMES: this reflex's wake threshold is a CONSTANT — `--threshold B bits`, a fixed CLI
    # arg (usage :25) compared against `score` with NO awareness of the current regime. So the same B both
    # floods minds during a legitimately churny window (operator arriving + devices appearing + arrivals
    # firing = lots of real surprisal that is EXPECTED given the volatility) AND can stay silent in a
    # dead-quiet period where a single odd event is the only thing that matters. The mesh already FELT this
    # as the novelty score-wobble flood ([[delta-channels-need-gate]]) — patched downstream with a static
    # --gate, never with a volatility-scaled bar. mesh-precision supplies a sense's precision (noise NOW);
    # NOTHING estimates volatility (change-rate OVER TIME) to set the threshold.
    #
    # DISTINCT from the three siblings on this file: (a) mesh-precision weights AMONG senses by signal noise
    # — orthogonal level (precision, not volatility); (b) the eigenform block ABOVE is the baseline ABSORBING
    # a persistent anomaly (a decoupling fixed point) — a first-order-MEAN pathology, whereas this is the
    # SECOND-ORDER VARIANCE setting an ADAPTIVE bar; (c) the reducible/irreducible-surprise block BELOW
    # (:136, Schmidhuber) is WHICH surprise is worth chasing — this is HOW MUCH surprise should wake, given
    # the regime. They compose: volatility scales the bar, aleatoric-discount picks the type, eigenform-drift
    # guards the baseline.
    # HELD FIX (instrument-first, steward/operator lands — behavioral, gates mind WAKE so validate first):
    # estimate recent volatility (rolling variance/EWMA of the surprisal series, or event-distribution
    # switch-rate over a short window) and SCALE the effective wake threshold by it — raise B in a volatile
    # window, lower it in a quiet one — so attention follows surprise-relative-to-regime, not raw bits. WHY
    # HELD: a volatility spike and a genuine regime change are degenerate at the signal level (same caveat as
    # the eigenform fix); a wrongly-low bar in a quiet window could chatter minds — needs a reference the
    # loop does not author. The mechanism is named here; the behavioral wiring is the steward's.
    # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    baseline = lines[:-window] if len(lines) > window else lines
    # baseline distribution over event types (add-1 / Laplace smoothing)
    base = Counter(event_type(l) for l in baseline)
    V = len(base) + 1                       # +1 for the unseen-type mass
    N = sum(base.values()) + V
    def p(t): return (base.get(t, 0) + 1) / N
    # CONDITIONAL (predictive-coding) mode: a first-order Markov forward model P(eᵢ|eᵢ₋₁) learnt
    # from the baseline transitions; surprise = -log P(eᵢ|eᵢ₋₁), the residual against the context
    # prediction. A context never seen as a predecessor backs off to the marginal p(t) (so it never
    # scores LESS surprising than marginal would). This "explains away" predictable sequences
    # (taking→done) while a contextually-unexpected transition stays high-bit.
    # ── NOISY-TV / REDUCIBLE vs IRREDUCIBLE SURPRISE (Schmidhuber; aleatoric≠epistemic) ──────────────
    # LITERATURE — information theory of agency (predictive information), the KNOWN FAILURE MODE
    # (2026-06-21): the NOISY-TV PROBLEM (Schmidhuber 1991, "A possibility for implementing curiosity
    # and boredom in model-building neural controllers"; named + measured by Burda, Edwards, Pathak et
    # al., "Large-Scale Study of Curiosity-Driven Learning", ICML 2019; Mavor-Parker et al., "How to
    # Stay Curious while Avoiding Noisy TVs using Aleatoric Uncertainty Estimation", ICML 2022; still
    # open per "Beyond Noisy-TVs: Noise-Robust Exploration via Learning Progress Monitoring",
    # arXiv:2509.25438, 2025). An agent that rewards RAW prediction error / information-gain fixates on
    # a STOCHASTIC source — TV static — that is endlessly "surprising" but UNLEARNABLE: the surprise is
    # IRREDUCIBLE (aleatoric) noise, not REDUCIBLE (epistemic) novelty, so observing it teaches nothing
    # yet pays maximal intrinsic reward forever. The principled fix is to value LEARNING PROGRESS —
    # the REDUCTION of prediction error over time (compression progress) — not the instantaneous error.
    # WHERE THIS REFLEX COMMITS THE GAP: BOTH scores here are instantaneous error. Marginal surprisal
    # -log P(e) and the --conditional residual -log P(e|prev) each score a source by how surprising it
    # is RIGHT NOW; NEITHER asks whether that surprise is FALLING as the baseline accumulates (learnable)
    # or PINNED high because the source is intrinsically random (a noisy-TV). Crucially --conditional does
    # NOT fix this: it explains away PREDICTABLE STRUCTURE (taking->done), but an aleatoric source HAS no
    # structure to explain away, so its conditional error stays maximal — by construction the predictive-
    # coding upgrade cannot reduce irreducible noise. So a genuinely random board source (a flapping
    # sensor's jittering event type, a metric that wobbles every window — the "novelty score-wobble
    # flood", [[delta-channels-need-gate]]) reads HIGH novelty EVERY window → use-case-2 ("wake on HIGH
    # novelty") wakes expensive minds on noise forever, and the digest top-5 (use-case-1) surfaces static.
    # That is the noisy-TV: this novelty SENSE is the curiosity reward, and it has no learnability filter.
    # HELD FIX (instrument-first, steward/operator lands — behavioral): a LEARNING-PROGRESS axis — track
    # an event type's surprisal across SUCCESSIVE windows; value a type whose surprise is DECLINING as it
    # accretes (epistemic — the model is learning it) and DISCOUNT a type whose surprise stays PINNED
    # high despite repeated exposure (aleatoric — a noisy-TV) before it can gate a SPEND/wake signal.
    # WHY HELD: estimating learnability needs a multi-window history this single-pass call does not keep,
    # and it must not discount a source that is high-surprise because it is genuinely NEW each window
    # (real ongoing novelty) vs random — separable only with a reducibility estimate validated against
    # board history. Gate nothing until validated (this is the mind-wake path). DISTINCT from the
    # EIGENFORM block above: that is a PERSISTENT anomaly ABSORBED into normal (surprise wrongly FALLS to
    # zero — a false NEGATIVE). Noisy-TV is the COMPLEMENT — irreducible noise NEVER absorbed (surprise
    # wrongly STAYS high — a false POSITIVE). Same missing ingredient (a learnability/reducibility read),
    # opposite error sign. NOT the --conditional explaining-away (handles structure, not stochasticity).
    # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    trans = {}
    if conditional:
        btypes = [event_type(l) for l in baseline]
        for a, b in zip(btypes, btypes[1:]):
            trans.setdefault(a, Counter())[b] += 1
    def p_cond(prev, cur):
        row = trans.get(prev)
        if row and sum(row.values()) > 0:
            cand = (row.get(cur, 0) + 1) / (sum(row.values()) + V)
            return min(cand, p(cur))        # never less surprising than the marginal floor
        return p(cur)                       # unseen context → marginal back-off
    # score the recent window
    scored = []
    start = len(lines) - len(recent)        # global index of recent[0] (for the predecessor)
    for i, l in enumerate(recent):
        t = event_type(l)
        if conditional:
            prev = event_type(lines[start + i - 1]) if start + i - 1 >= 0 else None
            bits = surprisal(p_cond(prev, t))
        else:
            bits = surprisal(p(t))
        novel = t not in base
        scored.append((bits, t, novel, l))
    scored.sort(reverse=True, key=lambda x: x[0])
    mean_bits = sum(s[0] for s in scored) / len(scored)
    # first-seen entities (categorical novelty): a device MAC newly observed by the
    # PRESENCE sense (~/.mesh/presence.log), never harvested from board prose — a MAC
    # merely *quoted* on the board (e.g. a synthetic test address) is not a device.
    # Split the presence log at the recent board window's start time; a baseline is
    # required, else nothing can be called "first-seen". Only a GLOBALLY-UNIQUE UNICAST
    # MAC is a stable real-world device identity worth flagging as a join: first octet
    # with BOTH the locally-administered bit (0x02) and the multicast bit (0x01) CLEAR.
    # Everything else rotates by design and phantoms into every window — classic
    # randomized BLE (0x02 set) AND BLE resolvable/non-resolvable private addresses that
    # carry the multicast bit (0x01) instead (e.g. 0x71 = a rotating RPA, ruled benign 3×
    # on 2026-06-12, evaded the old 0x02-only test). `& 0x03` catches both; no real OUI
    # device is excluded (real devices are always unicast+global → low 2 bits 0). Residual:
    # an RPA with both low bits clear can still slip — DHCP (mesh-lan-newdevice) is the
    # authoritative join sense; BLE presence is corroborating, not authoritative.
    new_macs = []
    pres = read_lines(PRESENCE)
    if pres and recent:
        t0 = recent[0].split(None, 1)[0]      # ISO-Z timestamps compare lexicographically
        hist = [l for l in pres if l.split(None, 1)[0] < t0]
        cur = [l for l in pres if l.split(None, 1)[0] >= t0]
        if hist:
            ephemeral = lambda m: int(m[:2], 16) & 0x03   # locally-administered OR multicast → not a stable device
            curtext = "\n".join(cur)
            hist_macs = {m.upper() for m in MAC.findall("\n".join(hist))}
            # PROXIMITY gate: a first-seen device is "novel" only if it's actually NEAR — a far BLE
            # blip (a neighbour's device drifting through walls, seen once at -95 dBm) is environmental
            # noise, not a presence event. Evidence (2026-06-12): 465 real non-ephemeral MACs in the
            # log, the bulk -86..-102 dBm seen once; the home's own devices sit at -54..-82. Gate at
            # MESH_NOVELTY_RSSI_MIN (default -85). Degrade safe: a MAC with NO parsed RSSI defaults to
            # the threshold → passes (only KNOWN-far devices are suppressed). DHCP (mesh-lan-newdevice)
            # stays the authoritative LAN-join sense; BLE is corroborating, not authoritative.
            near = int(os.environ.get("MESH_NOVELTY_RSSI_MIN", "-85"))
            best = {}
            for rssi, mac in re.findall(r'(-?\d+)\|([0-9A-Fa-f:]{17})', curtext):
                m = mac.upper(); r = int(rssi)
                if r > best.get(m, -999): best[m] = r
            new_macs = sorted(m for m in {x.upper() for x in MAC.findall(curtext)} - hist_macs
                              if not ephemeral(m) and best.get(m, near) >= near)
    # prior-preference floor: must-attend tags present in the recent window, WHATEVER their surprisal.
    # Kept separate from mean_bits/scored so the surprise MEASUREMENT stays pure (no silent inflation) —
    # this is a parallel, honestly-labelled attend-regardless channel, not a doctored novelty score.
    pref_hits = sorted({t for _, t, _, _ in scored if t in PREF_TAGS})
    # LOCAL-GLOBAL two-timescale deviance (report-only; see the LEVELS header block). GLOBAL baseline =
    # long history `base` (surprisal via p()); LOCAL baseline = the recent window MINUS its tip (the
    # immediate short-timescale context). Classify each DISTINCT type in the tip by the (global,local)
    # deviance pair — the dissociation the single-baseline `scored` cannot express.
    tip = min(LEVELS_TIP, len(recent))
    local_ctx = recent[:-tip] if tip < len(recent) else []
    lbase = Counter(event_type(l) for l in local_ctx)
    lN = sum(lbase.values()) + len(lbase) + 1
    def p_local(t):
        # empty local context → back off to the GLOBAL p (dissociation collapses: local==global).
        return ((lbase.get(t, 0) + 1) / lN) if local_ctx else p(t)
    levels = {}
    for l in recent[-tip:]:
        t = event_type(l)
        if t in levels:
            continue
        gs = surprisal(p(t)); ls = surprisal(p_local(t))
        gdev = gs >= LEVELS_HI; ldev = ls >= LEVELS_HI
        cls = ("REGIME-ONSET" if gdev and not ldev else   # global-deviant, local-standard: rare in history,
                                                          #   already recurring locally → anomaly forming
               "LOCAL-BLIP"   if ldev and not gdev else   # local-deviant, global-standard: routine type absent
                                                          #   from immediate context, reappearing → low wake value
               "BOTH-DEVIANT" if gdev and ldev else       # novel now AND historically
               "BASELINE")
        levels[t] = dict(cls=cls, gbits=round(gs, 2), lbits=round(ls, 2))
    # DETERRITORIALIZATION COEFFICIENT (D&G — see the header block). Split the recent window into an
    # EARLY half F and a LATE half S. For each type whose EARLY-half frequency ESCAPED above the long
    # baseline p(t) (a deterritorializing surge), κ = how much of that escape SURVIVED into the late half:
    #   κ = clamp( (late_freq − base) / (early_escape) , 0, 1 )
    # κ→0  the late half returned toward baseline → the surge was RECAPTURED → RELATIVE (a blip);
    # κ→1  the elevated rate HELD (or rose)        → not recaptured           → ABSOLUTE (a line of flight).
    half = len(recent) // 2
    F = Counter(event_type(l) for l in recent[:half])
    S = Counter(event_type(l) for l in recent[half:])
    nF = sum(F.values()) or 1
    nS = sum(S.values()) or 1
    territory = {}
    for t in set(F) | set(S):
        bp = p(t)                              # the long baseline — the type's territory
        fF = F.get(t, 0) / nF                  # early-half frequency
        fS = S.get(t, 0) / nS                  # late-half frequency
        escape = fF - bp                       # the deterritorializing edge (early)
        if escape <= ESCAPE_MIN:               # no significant escape → not a movement, skip
            continue
        persisted = fS - bp                    # how much of the escape survived the reterritorializing edge
        kappa = max(0.0, min(1.0, persisted / escape))
        territory[t] = dict(cls=("ABSOLUTE" if kappa >= 0.5 else "RELATIVE"),
                            kappa=round(kappa, 2), escape=round(escape, 3),
                            early=round(fF, 3), late=round(fS, 3), base=round(bp, 4))
    # ── BAYESIAN SURPRISE (Itti & Baldi) — belief-UPDATE, not improbability (report-only) ────────────
    # LITERATURE (live review 2026-07-28: predictive processing & the Bayesian brain — a foundational
    # idea this very file applied TOO LOOSELY, a SECOND time). The file's #2 payoff is a SPEND gate
    # ("wake on HIGH novelty") keyed on Shannon surprise −log P (marginal above, or --conditional's
    # −log P(e|prev)). Itti & Baldi's core empirical result is that raw improbability is the WRONG
    # attention signal: what attracts attention is BAYESIAN SURPRISE = KL[posterior‖prior], how much a
    # datum MOVES the observer's model — a quantity that can be ~0 for a very improbable event (it
    # changes no belief) and large for a probable one (it shifts beliefs). (Itti & Baldi, "Bayesian
    # surprise attracts human attention", NIPS 2005 / Vision Research 49(10):1295-1306, 2009; Baldi &
    # Itti, "Of bits and wows: A Bayesian theory of surprise with applications to attention", Neural
    # Networks 23(5), 2010. Still the live workhorse of curiosity/intrinsic-reward: "Curiosity-Driven
    # Exploration via Latent Bayesian Surprise", AAAI 2021; and 2024-25 active-inference exploration,
    # e.g. arXiv:2502.02962. Contrast the Schmidhuber block above, which asks WHICH surprise is worth
    # chasing (reducible vs noise) — this asks whether the surprise MOVES THE MODEL at all.)
    #
    # THE GAP: none of the axes above is Bayesian surprise. The `base` Counter IS already a Dirichlet
    # belief over event types (α = count+1, the same Laplace smoothing p() uses), so the KL of a single
    # observation is closed-form (bayes_bits()). The DISSOCIATION this surfaces on the mesh's own board:
    # a KNOWN-rare type ([incident],[health-fail]) scores ~6-8 Shannon bits EVERY recurrence → the raw
    # SPEND gate re-wakes minds each time — yet after the model has absorbed "rare things happen", the
    # 30th incident moves the belief ~0 (HABITUATED). Its belief-move only rebounds when the RATE shifts.
    # Each type is scored as a fraction of a BRAND-NEW type's belief-move at THIS corpus size (bs_new) —
    # corpus-calibrated, cannot saturate (per the pooled-rank doctrine), never an assumed 0..1 raw bar.
    # REPORT-ONLY / advisory, exactly like --levels/--territory/--independence: it does NOT replace the
    # Shannon SPEND gate nor the dark-room must-attend floor (a chronic critical condition must stay
    # attended even once its belief-move habituates — the two are complementary, not substitutes). It
    # names WHICH wakes raw surprisal over-pays; whether to skip one stays with the consumer.
    A_conc = N                                     # Dirichlet concentration = the smoothing p() already uses
    bs_new = bayes_bits(1.0, A_conc)               # reference: a brand-new type's belief-move at this corpus size
    bayesian = {}
    for t in {event_type(l) for l in recent}:
        alpha_t = base.get(t, 0) + 1.0
        bb = bayes_bits(alpha_t, A_conc)
        sb = surprisal(p(t))
        frac = (bb / bs_new) if bs_new > 0 else 0.0
        cls = ("MODEL-MOVING" if frac >= BAYES_FRAC else      # belief moves ≥ half a new type's → genuine attend
               "HABITUATED"   if sb >= LEVELS_HI else         # HIGH Shannon but belief no longer moves → over-wake
               "ROUTINE")                                     # low on both
        bayesian[t] = dict(cls=cls, bbits=round(bb, 3), sbits=round(sb, 2), frac=round(frac, 2))
    bayes_mean = (sum(bayesian[event_type(l)]["bbits"] for l in recent) / len(recent)) if recent else 0.0
    return dict(mean_bits=mean_bits, scored=scored, base=base, conditional=conditional,
                new_types=[t for _, t, n, _ in scored if n], new_macs=new_macs, pref_hits=pref_hits,
                levels=levels, levels_tip=tip, territory=territory,
                bayesian=bayesian, bayes_mean=bayes_mean, bayes_new_ref=round(bs_new, 3))

def diversity(base):
    """Shannon evenness (Pielou's J) of the RAW baseline type distribution — see the
    DIVERSITY docstring block above. Returns (H_bits, evenness 0..1, label). k<2 distinct
    types is trivially a monoculture (evenness undefined, reported as 0/DEGENERATE)."""
    total = sum(base.values())
    k = len(base)
    if k < 2 or total == 0:
        return (0.0, 0.0, "DEGENERATE")
    h = -sum((c / total) * math.log2(c / total) for c in base.values() if c > 0)
    j = h / math.log2(k)
    label = "DEGENERATE" if j < 0.35 else "FLAT" if j > 0.75 else "STRUCTURED"
    return (h, j, label)

def fmt(a):
    out = []
    pref = a.get('pref_hits') or []
    mode = "contextual prediction-error" if a.get('conditional') else "marginal surprise"
    verdict = ('NOVEL — worth a look' if a['mean_bits'] >= 4.0
               else ('routine · must-attend present' if pref else 'routine'))
    out.append(f"🔭 mesh-novelty — recent window mean {mode}: {a['mean_bits']:.2f} bits ({verdict})")
    top = [s for s in a['scored'] if s[0] >= 4.0][:5]
    if top:
        out.append("── most surprising recent events ──")
        for bits, t, novel, l in top:
            tagn = f"[{t}]" + (" NEW-TYPE" if novel else "")
            out.append(f"  {bits:4.1f}b {tagn}: {l[:90]}")
    # PRIOR-PREFERENCE FLOOR (dark-room): shown even when the window is "routine" — a chronic critical
    # type has LOW surprise (absorbed) yet must still be attended. Attended regardless of surprise.
    if pref:
        out.append("── must-attend (prior preference — attended regardless of surprise) ──")
        out.append("  " + " ".join(f"[{t}]" for t in pref)
                   + "  (dark-room floor: not explained away even once it becomes routine)")
    if a['new_macs']:
        out.append("── first-seen devices (novel presence) ──")
        for m in a['new_macs'][:5]:
            out.append(f"  + {m}")
    if not top and not a['new_macs'] and not pref:
        out.append("  (nothing surprising — the window is routine)")
    return "\n".join(out)

def _edge_decision(prev, mean, topN, min_gap, now):
    """Pure gate for --edge — returns (emit: bool, new_state | None).

    Fires when the novelty picture MATERIALLY changed since the last emit:
    a >±0.5b mean shift (score-band) OR a new entry in the top-5 composition.
    A non-zero min_gap adds a time FLOOR: a real edge inside the gap is held
    silent AND the baseline is left untouched (new_state=None), so the pending
    change still fires once the gap elapses — the floor delays, never swallows.
    This is the throttle the novelty-review cadence wants: a poster adopts
    `mesh-novelty --edge --min-gap 900` and posts only when this emits."""
    if prev:
        prev_top = prev.get("top5", prev.get("top3", []))   # back-compat w/ old state
        prev_mean = prev.get("mean", mean)
        if abs(mean - prev_mean) <= 0.5 and not any(t not in prev_top for t in topN):
            return (False, None)                            # no meaningful change
        if min_gap and (now - prev.get("emit_ts", 0)) < min_gap:
            return (False, None)                            # real edge, rate-floored
    return (True, {"mean": mean, "top5": topN, "emit_ts": now})

def main():
    args = sys.argv[1:]
    if "--test" in args:
        # self-test on a synthetic stream: a flood of routine + one rare event
        global read_lines
        sample = (["00:00:00Z a@n :: [done] x"] * 50
                  + ["00:00:00Z a@n :: [incident] something rare just happened"])
        _orig = read_lines
        read_lines = lambda p: sample if p == CHAT else []
        a = analyse(window=10)
        read_lines = _orig
        ok = a and any(t == "incident" for _, t, _, _ in a["scored"][:3])
        if not ok:
            print("smoke-test: FAIL (rare event not ranked surprising)"); sys.exit(1)
        # --edge gate: a real edge inside the min-gap is floored; the SAME edge after the
        # gap emits; an unchanged window is silent regardless of gap; back-compat top3 state.
        base = {"mean": 4.0, "top5": ["a", "b", "c", "d", "e"], "emit_ts": 1000}
        e_floor, _  = _edge_decision(base, 4.0, ["z", "b", "c", "d", "e"], 900, 1100)  # edge, 100s<900
        e_after, st = _edge_decision(base, 4.0, ["z", "b", "c", "d", "e"], 900, 2000)  # edge, 1000s>900
        e_same, _   = _edge_decision(base, 4.0, ["a", "b", "c", "d", "e"],   0, 9999)  # no change
        e_band, _   = _edge_decision(base, 4.7, ["a", "b", "c", "d", "e"],   0, 9999)  # +0.7b score-band
        e_compat, _ = _edge_decision({"mean": 4.0, "top3": ["a", "b", "c"]}, 4.0, ["z", "b", "c", "d", "e"], 0, 1)
        if not (e_floor is False and e_after is True and st.get("emit_ts") == 2000
                and e_same is False and e_band is True and e_compat is True):
            print(f"smoke-test: FAIL (edge gate floor={e_floor} after={e_after} "
                  f"same={e_same} band={e_band} compat={e_compat})"); sys.exit(1)
        # --conditional (predictive-coding) gate: baseline = STRICT taking↔done alternation, then a
        # SECOND [done] in a row appended. [done] is a marginally-common type (≈1 bit) so MARGINAL
        # scoring shrugs; but done-after-done never happens in context, so CONTEXTUAL scoring flags
        # it as high prediction error ("explaining away" the predictable, surfacing the unexpected).
        sample2 = (["00:00:00Z a@n :: [taking] x", "00:00:00Z a@n :: [done] x"] * 30
                   + ["00:00:00Z a@n :: [done] x"])
        read_lines = lambda p: sample2 if p == CHAT else []
        ac = analyse(window=10, conditional=True)
        am = analyse(window=10, conditional=False)
        read_lines = _orig
        ok2 = (ac and am and ac["scored"][0][1] == "done" and ac["scored"][0][0] > 3.0
               and am["scored"][0][0] < 2.0 and ac["mean_bits"] > am["mean_bits"])
        if not ok2:
            ct = ac["scored"][0] if ac else None; mt = am["scored"][0] if am else None
            print(f"smoke-test: FAIL (conditional gate: cond_top={ct} marg_top={mt})"); sys.exit(1)
        # --diversity: a monoculture (one type) is DEGENERATE; a Zipfian skew (few common +
        # long tail, like the real board) is STRUCTURED; a uniform spread is FLAT.
        mono = Counter({"done": 40})
        zipfy = Counter({"done": 50, "idle": 25, "taking": 12, "fyi": 6, "sense": 3, "incident": 1, "gap": 1})
        flat = Counter({t: 10 for t in "abcdefgh"})
        h_m, j_m, l_m = diversity(mono)
        h_z, j_z, l_z = diversity(zipfy)
        h_f, j_f, l_f = diversity(flat)
        ok3 = (l_m == "DEGENERATE" and j_m == 0.0 and l_z == "STRUCTURED" and l_f == "FLAT"
               and j_z < j_f)
        if not ok3:
            print(f"smoke-test: FAIL (diversity mono={l_m}/{j_m:.2f} zipf={l_z}/{j_z:.2f} flat={l_f}/{j_f:.2f})")
            sys.exit(1)
        # PRIOR-PREFERENCE FLOOR (dark-room): a chronic [health-fail] is ABSORBED into the baseline
        # (low marginal surprise, NOT a new type) — proving the boiling-frog failure is real — yet it
        # must still be surfaced as must-attend. Asserts BOTH: the absorption, and the floor catching it.
        sample4 = (["00:00:00Z a@n :: [done] x", "00:00:00Z a@n :: [health-fail] node down"] * 30)
        read_lines = lambda p: sample4 if p == CHAT else []
        ap = analyse(window=10)
        read_lines = _orig
        hf = [s for s in ap["scored"] if s[1] == "health-fail"]
        absorbed = bool(hf) and hf[0][0] < 4.0 and "health-fail" not in ap["new_types"]
        # NOTE the RED-first knob: MESH_NOVELTY_PREF_TAGS="" empties PREF_TAGS → pref_hits empty → FAIL.
        ok4 = absorbed and "health-fail" in ap.get("pref_hits", [])
        if not ok4:
            print(f"smoke-test: FAIL (prior-preference floor: absorbed={absorbed} "
                  f"pref_hits={ap.get('pref_hits')} hf_bits={hf[0][0] if hf else None})"); sys.exit(1)
        # LOCAL-GLOBAL two-timescale deviance: build a stream where the SAME single-baseline surprisal
        # cannot tell two recent-tip types apart, but the local/global split can.
        #   [deploy] is ABSENT from long history yet fills the immediate local context (recurring) →
        #            global-deviant + local-standard → REGIME-ONSET (an anomaly forming, pre-absorption).
        #   [done]  is COMMON in long history but ABSENT from the immediate local context, reappearing at
        #            the tip → global-standard + local-deviant → LOCAL-BLIP (routine oddball, low wake).
        # RED-first knob: MESH_NOVELTY_LEVELS_TIP>=window empties the LOCAL context → p_local backs off to
        # the GLOBAL p → local==global → deploy reads BOTH-DEVIANT and done reads BASELINE → this FAILS.
        sample5 = (["00:00:00Z a@n :: [done] x"] * 60
                   + ["00:00:00Z a@n :: [deploy] a"] * 20
                   + ["00:00:00Z a@n :: [deploy] a", "00:00:00Z a@n :: [done] x",
                      "00:00:00Z a@n :: [deploy] a", "00:00:00Z a@n :: [done] x",
                      "00:00:00Z a@n :: [deploy] a"])
        read_lines = lambda p: sample5 if p == CHAT else []
        al = analyse(window=25)
        read_lines = _orig
        lv = (al or {}).get("levels", {})
        ok5 = (lv.get("deploy", {}).get("cls") == "REGIME-ONSET"
               and lv.get("done", {}).get("cls") == "LOCAL-BLIP")
        if not ok5:
            print(f"smoke-test: FAIL (local-global levels: deploy={lv.get('deploy')} "
                  f"done={lv.get('done')} — want deploy=REGIME-ONSET, done=LOCAL-BLIP)"); sys.exit(1)
        # DETERRITORIALIZATION COEFFICIENT (D&G): two types both SURGE in the early half of the window
        # (both absent from the long baseline → both escape), but they differ in RECAPTURE:
        #   [flight] persists at the same elevated rate into the LATE half → not recaptured → ABSOLUTE.
        #   [blip]   vanishes in the late half (board returns toward baseline) → recaptured → RELATIVE.
        # Magnitude alone cannot tell them apart (identical early surprise); only the late-half recapture
        # read does. RED-first knob: MESH_NOVELTY_ESCAPE_MIN=1.0 makes NO surge clear the escape floor →
        # territory empties → both assertions go red.
        sample6 = (["00:00:00Z a@n :: [done] x"] * 80
                   + ["00:00:00Z a@n :: [flight] a", "00:00:00Z a@n :: [blip] b"] * 5   # early half: both surge
                   + ["00:00:00Z a@n :: [flight] a", "00:00:00Z a@n :: [done] x"] * 5)  # late half: flight holds, blip gone
        read_lines = lambda p: sample6 if p == CHAT else []
        at = analyse(window=20)
        read_lines = _orig
        tv = (at or {}).get("territory", {})
        ok6 = (tv.get("flight", {}).get("cls") == "ABSOLUTE"
               and tv.get("blip", {}).get("cls") == "RELATIVE"
               and tv["flight"]["kappa"] > tv["blip"]["kappa"])
        if not ok6:
            print(f"smoke-test: FAIL (deterritorialization: flight={tv.get('flight')} "
                  f"blip={tv.get('blip')} — want flight=ABSOLUTE, blip=RELATIVE)"); sys.exit(1)
        # BAYESIAN SURPRISE (Itti & Baldi): the dissociation Shannon surprise cannot express. A stream
        # where [incident] is KNOWN-rare (30 in the long baseline → HIGH Shannon every recurrence, but
        # the belief has absorbed "rare things happen" → ~0 belief-move → HABITUATED) vs [surge], a
        # brand-new type at the tip (first sighting → maximal belief-move → MODEL-MOVING). BOTH are
        # high-Shannon; only Bayesian surprise separates the wasted wake from the genuine one.
        # RED-first knob: replacing bayes_bits() with surprisal() (belief-move → improbability) makes
        # incident's frac clear BAYES_FRAC → it reads MODEL-MOVING → this FAILS. Plus a digamma anchor.
        sample7 = (["00:00:00Z a@n :: [done] x"] * 2000
                   + ["00:00:00Z a@n :: [incident] known rare"] * 30
                   + ["00:00:00Z a@n :: [done] x"] * 6
                   + ["00:00:00Z a@n :: [incident] recurs",
                      "00:00:00Z a@n :: [surge] never seen before"])
        read_lines = lambda p: sample7 if p == CHAT else []
        ab = analyse(window=10)
        read_lines = _orig
        bv = (ab or {}).get("bayesian", {})
        inc = bv.get("incident", {}); sur = bv.get("surge", {})
        dg1 = _digamma(1.0); dg2 = _digamma(2.0)
        ok7 = (inc.get("cls") == "HABITUATED" and sur.get("cls") == "MODEL-MOVING"
               and inc.get("sbits", 0) >= LEVELS_HI                       # incident IS high Shannon surprise
               and sur.get("bbits", 0) > inc.get("bbits", 9) * 3          # yet the new type moves belief far more
               and abs(dg1 - (-0.5772156649)) < 1e-3                      # ψ(1) = −γ  (formula anchor)
               and abs(dg2 - 0.4227843351) < 1e-3)                       # ψ(2) = 1−γ
        if not ok7:
            print(f"smoke-test: FAIL (bayesian surprise: incident={inc} surge={sur} "
                  f"dg1={dg1:.5f} dg2={dg2:.5f} — want incident=HABITUATED hi-Shannon, "
                  f"surge=MODEL-MOVING, bbits(surge)>3·bbits(incident))"); sys.exit(1)
        print("smoke-test: ok"); sys.exit(0)
    window = 40
    if "--window" in args:
        try: window = int(args[args.index("--window") + 1])
        except (ValueError, IndexError): pass
    cond = "--conditional" in args or "--ctx" in args
    a = analyse(window=window, conditional=cond)
    if a is None:
        print("mesh-novelty: not enough history yet"); return
    if "--diversity" in args:
        h, j, label = diversity(a["base"])
        print(f"novelty-diversity[{label}]: H={h:.2f}b evenness={j:.2f} "
              f"types={len(a['base'])} (Zipfian codes sit low-mid; near-0=monoculture, near-1=unstructured)")
        return
    if "--levels" in args:
        lv = a["levels"]
        if "--json" in args:
            import json
            print(json.dumps(dict(levels_tip=a["levels_tip"], levels=lv), sort_keys=True))
            return
        order = sorted(lv.items(), key=lambda kv: -kv[1]["gbits"])
        body = ", ".join(f"[{t}] {d['cls']} (global {d['gbits']}b / local {d['lbits']}b)" for t, d in order)
        print(f"novelty-levels (local-global, tip={a['levels_tip']}): "
              + (body or "baseline — no recent deviants"))
        onset = [t for t, d in lv.items() if d["cls"] == "REGIME-ONSET"]
        if onset:
            print("  REGIME-ONSET " + " ".join(f"[{t}]" for t in onset)
                  + " = rare in long history yet ALREADY RECURRING locally — an anomaly forming BEFORE"
                    " the baseline absorbs it (the eigenform-absorption complement, caught at onset).")
        return
    if "--territory" in args:
        tv = a["territory"]
        if "--json" in args:
            import json
            print(json.dumps(tv, sort_keys=True))
            return
        order = sorted(tv.items(), key=lambda kv: -kv[1]["kappa"])
        body = ", ".join(f"[{t}] {d['cls']} (κ={d['kappa']}, escape+{d['escape']}, "
                         f"early {d['early']}→late {d['late']} vs base {d['base']})" for t, d in order)
        print("novelty-territory (deterritorialization coefficient — relative=recaptured / "
              "absolute=line of flight): " + (body or "no deterritorializing surge in window"))
        flight = [t for t, d in tv.items() if d["cls"] == "ABSOLUTE"]
        if flight:
            print("  ABSOLUTE " + " ".join(f"[{t}]" for t in flight)
                  + " = a surge that was NOT recaptured — the board's distribution did not return to its"
                    " prior shape (a line of flight / new regime), vs a RELATIVE surge that snapped back.")
        return
    if "--bayesian" in args or "--wow" in args:
        bv = a["bayesian"]
        if "--json" in args:
            import json
            print(json.dumps(dict(bayes_mean=round(a["bayes_mean"], 3),
                                  bayes_new_ref=a["bayes_new_ref"], bayesian=bv), sort_keys=True))
            return
        order = sorted(bv.items(), key=lambda kv: -kv[1]["bbits"])
        body = ", ".join(f"[{t}] {d['cls']} (Δbelief {d['bbits']}b vs surprise {d['sbits']}b — "
                         f"{int(d['frac']*100)}% of a new type)" for t, d in order)
        print("novelty-bayesian (Itti & Baldi — attention follows belief-UPDATE, not improbability; "
              f"window Δbelief {a['bayes_mean']:.3f}b): " + (body or "baseline"))
        hab = [t for t, d in bv.items() if d["cls"] == "HABITUATED"]
        if hab:
            print("  HABITUATED " + " ".join(f"[{t}]" for t in hab)
                  + " = HIGH Shannon surprise but the belief no longer MOVES — a wake the raw-surprisal"
                    " SPEND gate would pay every recurrence, that Bayesian surprise says skip.")
        mm = [t for t, d in bv.items() if d["cls"] == "MODEL-MOVING"]
        if mm:
            print("  MODEL-MOVING " + " ".join(f"[{t}]" for t in mm)
                  + " = the datum shifts the mesh's model of its own event distribution — genuine attend.")
        return
    if "--edge" in args:
        import json  # `time` is module-level (used by the --threshold prior-preference gate too)
        edgef = os.path.join(MESH, ".novelty-edge-state")
        min_gap = 0  # opt-in min-interval floor (seconds); 0 = unrated (existing default)
        if "--min-gap" in args:
            try: min_gap = int(args[args.index("--min-gap") + 1])
            except (ValueError, IndexError): min_gap = 0
        try:
            prev = json.load(open(edgef))
        except (OSError, ValueError):
            prev = None
        topN = [s[1] for s in a["scored"][:5]]   # top-5 composition (was top-3)
        emit, state = _edge_decision(prev, a["mean_bits"], topN, min_gap, int(time.time()))
        if not emit:
            return  # no meaningful change, or a real edge held by the min-gap floor
        json.dump(state, open(edgef, "w"))
        print(fmt(a))
        return
    if "--threshold" in args:
        try: thr = float(args[args.index("--threshold") + 1])
        except (ValueError, IndexError): thr = 4.0
        # stream mode: emit a feed line only when the window is genuinely novel.
        # Label HONESTLY by which signal fired — saying "new device" on a board-surprise
        # event with no MAC sent minds device-hunting 3× on 2026-06-12. A real device join
        # is named only when new_macs is actually non-empty.
        # DEDUP (2026-06-13): a first-seen device re-fires every window until it ages into the
        # baseline — the SAME MAC re-flagged 3× (64:A4:C0, escalating 4.1→4.5b), re-waking minds.
        # Only a FRESH (not-yet-flagged) MAC counts for the device fire; remember flagged MACs
        # (recency-capped 500, so a long-departed device can re-alert later).
        # DEDUP (2026-06-15): same problem exists for new_types — a first-seen tag fires every
        # 10-min cron cycle until it ages into the baseline (e.g. [void]/[decommission] burst
        # re-fired twice). Fixed: same flagged-file pattern, cap-500, fires once per new tag.
        flagf = os.path.join(MESH, ".novelty-flagged-macs")
        try: prev_flagged = open(flagf).read().split()
        except OSError: prev_flagged = []
        flagged_set = set(prev_flagged)
        fresh_macs = [m for m in a["new_macs"] if m not in flagged_set]

        typef = os.path.join(MESH, ".novelty-flagged-types")
        try: prev_types = open(typef).read().split()
        except OSError: prev_types = []
        flagged_types = set(prev_types)
        fresh_types = [t for t in a["new_types"] if t not in flagged_types]

        # PRIOR-PREFERENCE FLOOR (dark-room fix — see header): must-attend tags fire regardless of
        # surprise. Deduped by TIME (re-assert every PREF_REFRESH), not once-then-silent — so a chronic
        # critical condition is never permanently explained away (the boiling-frog failure) nor spammed
        # each cron cycle. This is the ONE place absorption is unblocked, and only for the design-set.
        preff = os.path.join(MESH, ".novelty-pref-fired")
        pref_last = {}
        try:
            for ln in open(preff):
                parts = ln.split()
                if len(parts) == 2: pref_last[parts[0]] = float(parts[1])
        except OSError: pass
        now_s = time.time()
        fresh_pref = [t for t in a.get("pref_hits", []) if now_s - pref_last.get(t, 0) >= PREF_REFRESH]

        # "routine type spiking" (no new type/device) is low-value by design — raise the bar
        # so a quiet score wobble (4.6→5.4b) doesn't keep waking the mind. Real novelty signals
        # (fresh_types or fresh_macs) fire at the normal threshold regardless.
        spike_thr = thr + 2.0  # 6.0b default for the routine-spike case
        fires = bool(fresh_macs or fresh_types or fresh_pref or a["mean_bits"] >= spike_thr)
        if fires:
            if fresh_pref:
                what = "must-attend " + ','.join('[' + t + ']' for t in fresh_pref[:3]) \
                       + " (prior-preference floor — attended regardless of surprise)"
            elif fresh_types:
                what = ','.join('[' + t + ']' for t in fresh_types[:3])
            elif fresh_macs:
                what = "new device " + fresh_macs[0]
            else:
                what = "high board surprise (no new event-type/device — a routine type spiking)"
            print(f"novelty[{a['mean_bits']:.1f}b]: unusual mesh activity — {what} — look + react")
            if fresh_macs:
                kept = (prev_flagged + fresh_macs)[-500:]
                try:
                    with open(flagf, "w") as f: f.write("\n".join(kept))
                except OSError: pass
            if fresh_types:
                kept = (prev_types + fresh_types)[-500:]
                try:
                    with open(typef, "w") as f: f.write("\n".join(kept))
                except OSError: pass
            if fresh_pref:
                for t in fresh_pref: pref_last[t] = now_s
                try:
                    with open(preff, "w") as f:
                        f.write("\n".join(f"{k} {v:.0f}" for k, v in pref_last.items()))
                except OSError: pass
        return
    print(fmt(a))

if __name__ == "__main__":
    main()
